<p>Checked on 24 October 2026. <a href="/review/relational-collection/evidence/r34/plan-repairs.sql/" download="plan-repairs.sql">Download the plan-repair worksheet</a> and run <code>psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -f plan-repairs.sql</code> in a disposable database. The complete file ran on a private PostgreSQL 18.6 instance. It uses temporary synthetic relations, disables parallel gathering for legible comparisons, forces the two stated plan modes and resets both changes. Counts and estimates in the article are observed; the proof diagram is explanatory. No automatic-plan-switch or production-latency claim is made.</p>
